<title>CHILE: YPF to supply Chile's Endesa plant.</title>
<headline>YPF to supply Chile's Endesa plant.</headline>
<dateline>SANTIAGO 1996-10-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chilean power company Empresa Nacional de Electricidad SA (Endesa) said it signed a $350 million contract under which Argentine energy company YPF SA will supply natural gas to its planned San Isidro plant.</p>
<p>The 15-year deal involves the supply of 1.8 million cubic meters of natural gas a day to the San Isidro power station to be built in central Chile, said Endesa in a statement.</p>
<p>The gas will be pumped across the Andes to Chile using a gas pipeline being built from Mendoza in central Argentina to Santiago. It is due to be completed next year.</p>
<p>--Margaret Orgill, Santiago newsroom, 562-699-5595 x212</p>
